bin/
.env
*.log
# The binary a bare `go build` leaves at go-server/gameplay (ops/build.sh
# writes bin/ instead). Anchored: unanchored it also matched cmd/gameplay/,
# which hid every new file there from git.
/gameplay

# Service-account keys. GOOGLE_PLAY_CREDENTIALS_FILE points at one of these and
# it lives next to the binary, inside a tracked directory — so the ignore rule
# is what stands between a private key and the public repository. Match by
# shape, not by one filename, because the next one will be called something
# else.
play-key.json
*-key.json
*.serviceaccount.json
